{# "Edit this bit of the chrome", shown on the bit itself.

   The navbar, the banner and the footer are the three things people ask how to change, and
   until now the answer was a route or a page name you had to be told (ticket 30 exists
   because of exactly that). A pencil where the thing is says it without being told.

   Icon only, with the label as its accessible name: this sits inside the wiki's own chrome
   on every page, and a labelled button there would compete with the site's actual
   navigation. It is only rendered for someone who may follow it -- TemplateEngine checks
   before this template is reached, so there is no disabled state to explain. #}
<a class="yw-chrome-edit" href="{{ href }}" title="{{ label }}" aria-label="{{ label }}">
  {{ icon('pencil') }}
</a>
